    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 4.2.6 and Annex B, and ISO 19650-3 A.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Annex B codes 323 unintended collapse, 333 machinery guarding, 334 loss of control, 353 struck by machinery or part and 354 overturning plant or moving machinery are all direct consequences of equipment or structural failure, so an asset failure mode is one of the ways a recordable health and safety incident is produced. This is the edge that lets the effectiveness of a predictive maintenance programme be measured on a safety metric rather than only on downtime." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_incident ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESULTS_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_failure_mode .

iso:rel_106 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.1; 5.1.9; Figure 3 (1)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_im_process_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_assessment_and_need_delivery .

iso:rel_1060 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 4.2.2 a) and Annex B, and ISO 19650-3 A.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The prospective counterpart of the edge above: a known failure mode is one of the sources of a health and safety risk that shall be documented under 4.2.4." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_risk ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CONTRIBUTES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_failure_mode .

iso:rel_1061 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 4.2.6, 4.3.4 and 6.2, and ISO 19650-3 A.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "6.2 requires the appointing party to consider 'the potential for parties to automatically extract information on relevant incidents', which is exactly the ingestion path a predictive maintenance model needs. Incident records carry Associated product, activity and location, so they resolve to the same asset the condition data is measured on." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_pdm_model ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_incident .

iso:rel_1062 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 4.2.6 and ISO 19650-3 A.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "4.2.6 requires ALL incidents to be recorded including near miss events. Near misses are precisely the pre-failure signals with the highest predictive value and the ones most often lost, so this requirement is the single most valuable normative provision of Part 6 for predictive maintenance." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_pdm_model ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_near_miss .

iso:rel_1063 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 4.2.6 and ISO 19650-3 A.4.2, A.4.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "A near miss and an anomaly event are the same object seen from two sides: an observed deviation from expected behaviour that did not produce harm. Matching them lets a model-detected anomaly be validated against a human-reported near miss on the same asset and time window." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_anomaly_event ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CORRESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_near_miss .

iso:rel_1064 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 4.3.4 and Table 3, and ISO 19650-3 A.4.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Because the incident sub-schema mirrors the risk sub-schema on the same product/activity/location triple, an incident that has occurred can be matched directly against a risk registered beforehand, which measures how many predicted risks actually materialized." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_failure_history ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CONTRIBUTES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_incident .

iso:rel_1065 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 4.3.8 and Annex C, and ISO 19650-3 A.4.2, A.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "4.3.8 requires the outcome of a risk assessment 'using any appropriate method' to be communicated, which admits condition-derived assessment; Annex C then supplies the encoding." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_level_of_risk ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_condition_observation .

iso:rel_1066 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 Annex C Table C.1 and ISO 19650-3 A.2-A.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "An assessed asset health value is a quantitative estimate of the likelihood grade that Table C.1 asks to be recorded as a five-level enumeration." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_likelihood ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_indicator .

iso:rel_1067 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 Annex C Table C.1 and ISO 19650-3 A.2, 5.2.2 Note 1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Remaining useful life is a time-to-failure estimate, so within a stated horizon it maps onto the likelihood grade; the horizon has to be stated for the mapping to be meaningful." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_likelihood ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_remaining_useful_life_prediction .

iso:rel_1068 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 Annex C Table C.3 and ISO 19650-3 5.1.5, A.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Table C.3 maps the five risk levels onto very urgent, urgent, short term, medium term and long term prioritization during operations. That is an alert priority scale, so a predictive maintenance alert can be graded on the same scale as the health and safety register rather than on a separate one." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_maintenance_alert ;
    rdf:predicate iso:GOVERNS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_risk_urgency_prioritization .

iso:rel_1069 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 4.3.5 and Table 4, and ISO 19650-3 A.3-A.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Both scheduled preventive maintenance and condition-based maintenance are engineering controls under the Table 4 Category enumeration, so a work order can be registered as a risk treatment record - inheriting Risk links, Incident links, Approved by and Review date." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_treatment_control ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CORRESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_maintenance_work_order .

iso:rel_107 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.2; 5.2.5; Figure 3 (2)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_im_process_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_invitation_to_tender_delivery .

iso:rel_1070 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 4.5.1 and 4.5.2, and ISO 19650-3 5.1.12, A.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "4.5.1 requires health and safety information to be reviewed for changes whenever the information model is modified. A completed intervention is such a modification: it closes or re-grades the risk it treated and can create a new incident record if the intervention revealed one." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_register ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CONTRIBUTES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_maintenance_intervention_outcome .

iso:rel_1071 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 4.3.6 NOTE and ISO 19650-3 A.4.2, A.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The 4.3.6 NOTE is the only place in the whole ISO 19650 series that ties information properties to specific measurable engineering quantities - deflection limits and load capacities - and states that they enable 'active near-real-time digital monitoring techniques'." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_condition_observation ;
    rdf:predicate iso:ENABLES ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_properties .

iso:rel_1072 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 4.3.6 and ISO 19650-3 A.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "4.3.6 requires properties to be documented throughout the asset life cycle and to be incorporated for 'automated queries', which is a rare normative requirement for machine queryability." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_pdm_model ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_properties .

iso:rel_1073 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 4.3.2 Table 1 and ISO 19650-3 A.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "'Entries shall not be deleted' makes the risk and incident record append-only, which is the immutability property a training set needs if model performance is to be reproducible." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_pdm_model ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:field_history .

iso:rel_1074 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 4.3.3 Table 2 and ISO 19650-3 A.4.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The Associated product field accepts a model entity reference, and the unique asset identifier is what that reference resolves to. Without this join the health and safety register and the condition record describe the same equipment under two unrelated keys." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_unique_identifier ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:field_associated_product .

iso:rel_1075 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "mapped from ISO 19650-6 Introduction and ISO 19650-3 A.3, A.4.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "USE-CASE EXTENSION" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The Introduction states that one important use of incident information is to link incidents to design factors so that designers learn how their designed assets perform in use. Accumulated across projects that is a failure mode catalogue." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_failure_mode ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CONTRIBUTES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_design_factor_learning .

iso:rel_1076 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.3 c) 3)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "5.4.3 c) 3) requires consideration of information 'to enable the safe repair, maintenance or replacement of plant and equipment including assumptions' - the most explicitly maintenance-facing requirement in Part 6." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_maintenance_work_order ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_1077 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.3 c) 1)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "5.4.3 c) 1) covers maintenance and operation methods, constructability and operability and critical sequences, which is what an inspection and maintenance schedule is built from." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_maintenance_inspection_schedule ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_1078 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.1 b)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "5.1 b) requires the organizational information requirements to state the 'connections required to facilitate use of the health and safety information with other datasets'. The CAFM/asset management system is the dataset a maintenance-driven use case has to connect to." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_cafm_system ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_register .

iso:rel_1079 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.1 b)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The general form of the previous edge; ISO 19650-3, 5.1.10 requires information quality and security processes to be established in any enterprise system linked into the AIM, which applies to the health and safety register as much as to any other content." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_enterprise_system ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_register .

iso:rel_108 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.3; 5.3.8; Figure 3 (3)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_im_process_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_tender_response_delivery .

iso:rel_1080 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex B" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Codes 323, 333, 334, 353 and 354 are the equipment-failure subset of the safety issue group, i.e. the incident codes a predictive maintenance programme is aiming to drive down." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_failure_mode ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_classification_safety .

iso:rel_1081 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "4.5.4 requires each appointed party to review whether its proposals are buildable AND MAINTAINABLE. Maintainability is a design parameter, so this is where operational-phase maintenance feasibility is fed back into design decisions." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_design_parameters ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_buildability_maintainability_review .

iso:rel_1082 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.3; 4.5.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "3.3 defines generalization as removing or modifying details to make information suitable for wider publication and re-use, and Note 1 says this can include replacing personal and protected characteristics. That is redaction and protective formatting under ISO 19650-5, reached from the opposite direction: Part 5 redacts to deny an attacker, Part 6 generalizes to enable industry-wide learning, but the operation on the record is the same." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_redaction ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CORRESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_generalization .

iso:rel_1083 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.3; Table 2; 4.3.4; Table 3; Annex A; Table A.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Tables 2 and 3 note 'Privacy can need protection' against Affected party, Raised by and Owned by, and footnote b of Table A.1 states that organizational, project or role based identification can be used in preference to personal identification. That footnote is a protective formatting rule written into the schema itself." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_redaction ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:field_affected_party .

iso:rel_1084 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.2; Table 1; 4.3.3; Table 2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "CONFLICT TO RESOLVE AT IMPLEMENTATION. ISO 19650-6 states 'Entries shall not be deleted' for the History field of all four sub-schemas, while the generic information lifecycle of ISO 19650-5 includes purging. Both are normative in their own document, so an implementation has to reconcile them - typically by purging the payload while retaining the append-only audit entry, or by scoping the no-deletion rule to the register and the purge rule to derived copies. This matters for predictive maintenance because the training history is the thing both rules bite on." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_lifecycle_purging ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:field_history .

iso:rel_1085 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.2; Table 1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "An append-only history of incidents and risks carrying Associated location and dates is itself pattern-of-use information about the asset, which ISO 19650-5 treats as sensitive. The same is true of the condition time series a predictive maintenance programme accumulates, so the security triage has to be applied to the health and safety register and not only to the geometric model." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_pattern_of_use ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:field_history .

iso:rel_1086 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex B; 4.2.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Annex B code 41 'Connected plant and machinery' is the only sub-code under the security issue group, and connected plant is precisely what the ISO 19650-5 internet of things assessment covers. For predictive maintenance this is the same equipment twice over: the sensors that supply the condition data are themselves the connected plant that carries the security risk." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_iot_security_assessment ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_classification_security .

iso:rel_1087 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.2.2 NOTE; 4.3.3; Table 2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The NOTE to 4.2.2 says 'Other types of risk can be managed using this method without collaborative sharing.' That is an explicit invitation to carry an ISO 19650-5 security risk in the Table 2 risk schema - and an explicit withdrawal of the 4.5.2 duty to share it with all parties. One schema, two sharing regimes, decided by the risk type." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_risk_sub_schema ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_security_risk .

iso:rel_1088 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.2; 4.5.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "CONFLICT TO RESOLVE AT IMPLEMENTATION. ISO 19650-6, 4.5.2 requires all parties to 'share ALL generated health and safety information with ALL parties', while ISO 19650-5 requires an assessment before any new, modified or existing information is shared or published. 4.5.5 acknowledges the tension in one phrase - 'whilst remaining security-minded' - but sets no precedence. On a sensitive built asset the assessment has to run first and the sharing duty is met with generalized information; see also the append-only versus purging conflict on field_history." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_third_party_information_provision_assessment ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_information_sharing .

iso:rel_1089 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.1; 4.5.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "4.3.1 requires the health and safety information provided to meet the necessary integrity, availability and confidentiality requirements, and 4.5.2 puts the register in the CDE. The security information requirements are what state which of its contents count as sensitive. ISO 19650-5 already governs every node of the ISO 19650-3 predictive maintenance loop this way; this edge extends the same governance to the health and safety register that feeds it." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_register ;
    rdf:predicate iso:GOVERNS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_security_information_requirements .

iso:rel_109 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4; 5.4.8; Figure 3 (4)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_im_process_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_appointment_delivery .

iso:rel_1090 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.2.6; Annex B" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Annex B group 4 'Security issue', with its single sub-code 41 'Connected plant and machinery', means a security breach involving connected plant is recordable as a health and safety incident under 4.2.6. The two registers overlap but must not be merged: the ISO 19650-5 breach response has its own immediate-notification path and its own containment and recovery steps, which the health and safety incident schema does not model." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_security_breach_discovery_response ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_incident .

iso:rel_1091 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "4.5.5 requires the appointing party to keep health and safety information available throughout the asset life cycle 'whilst remaining security-minded'. The sensitivity assessment is the process that decides what that means for a given asset, so it is the gate on the availability duty." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_sensitivity_assessment ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_1092 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.3; Table 2; 4.3.4; Table 3; Annex A; Table A.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "A register of Affected party plus Associated location plus dates is an aggregation risk in the ISO 19650-5 sense even when no single entry is sensitive: taken together the entries can identify individuals or reveal a pattern of use. Footnote b of Table A.1 - prefer organizational, project or role based identification over personal identification - is the schema-level mitigation." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_aggregation_risk ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:field_affected_party .

iso:rel_1093 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.1; 4.3.6 NOTE" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The 4.3.6 NOTE has health and safety properties enabling active near-real-time digital monitoring, and 4.3.1 requires integrity, availability and confidentiality to be considered for the information so provided. Technological security controls are what ISO 19650-5 puts on the systems capturing, processing and storing that information." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_technological_security_control ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_properties .

iso:rel_1094 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.2; Table 1; 4.3.3; Table 2; 4.3.4; Table 3; 4.3.5; Table 4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Tables 1 to 4 define Associated location as 'space, location, zone or site', so the field carries the ISO 19650-1 concept of space (3.1.2) and can hold a model entity reference to one. This is the spatial half of the product-activity-location axis: it is what lets a risk or an incident be resolved to a zone rather than only to a component." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_space ;
    rdf:predicate iso:DESCRIBES ;
    rdf:subject iso:field_associated_location .

iso:rel_11 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.7; 12.1; Figure 2; Figure 3 point C" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Figure 2 states that the PIM 'contributes to' the AIM. At the end of a project, only the information containers required for asset management are moved from the PIM to the AIM; this relationship must not be interpreted as aggregation of the entire PIM into the AIM." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_aim ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CONTRIBUTES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_pim .

iso:rel_110 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.5; 5.5.4; Figure 3 (5)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_im_process_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_mobilization_delivery .

iso:rel_111 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.6; 5.6.6; Figure 3 (6)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_im_process_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_collaborative_production_of_information_delivery .

iso:rel_112 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.7; 5.7.5; Figure 3 (7)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_im_process_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_information_model_delivery .

iso:rel_113 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8; 5.8.3; Figure 3 (8)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_im_process_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_project_close_out_delivery .

iso:rel_114 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Figure 3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Figure 3 NOTE 2: the order in which activities are presented reflects the order in which they are undertaken. Activity 1 is undertaken per project (grouping B); activities 2-7 recur per appointment (grouping C)." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_invitation_to_tender_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PRECEDES ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_assessment_and_need_delivery .

iso:rel_115 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Figure 3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Both within grouping D - activities undertaken during the procurement stage of each appointment." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_tender_response_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PRECEDES ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_invitation_to_tender_delivery .

iso:rel_116 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Figure 3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_appointment_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PRECEDES ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_tender_response_delivery .

iso:rel_117 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Figure 3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Both within grouping E - activities undertaken during the information planning stage of each appointment." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_mobilization_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PRECEDES ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_appointment_delivery .

iso:rel_118 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Figure 3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_collaborative_production_of_information_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PRECEDES ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_mobilization_delivery .

iso:rel_119 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Figure 3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Both within grouping F - activities undertaken during the information production stage of each appointment." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_information_model_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PRECEDES ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_collaborative_production_of_information_delivery .

iso:rel_12 a rdf:Statement ;
