iso:rel_182 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.2.3; 5.3.7; Figure 3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The tender response shall meet the tender response requirements established by the appointing party in 5.2.3 and issued within the invitation to tender package." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_invitation_to_tender_information ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_delivery_team_tender_response .

iso:rel_183 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "REUSES the Part 3 node. Identifies what information is to be produced, when it is to be exchanged and with whom, and which task team is responsible for its production; considering the information delivery milestones, the high-level responsibility matrix, the project's information production methods and procedures, the elements of information container breakdown structure allocated to each task team, and the dependencies on the information production process." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_detailed_responsibility_matrix ;
    rdf:predicate iso:ESTABLISHES ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_lead_appointed_party .

iso:rel_184 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The lead appointed party shall FURTHER REFINE the high-level responsibility matrix to establish the detailed responsibility matrix." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_high_level_responsibility_matrix ;
    rdf:predicate iso:DERIVED_FROM ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_detailed_responsibility_matrix .

iso:rel_185 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The lead appointed party establishes its own EIR for each appointed party, defining each information requirement considering both the appointing party's information requirements that it requires the appointed party to meet and any additional information requirements of its own. When engaging internal teams it is recommended that a clear schedule of information requirements is established as though it was a formal appointment." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_eir_iso19650_2 ;
    rdf:predicate iso:ESTABLISHES ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_lead_appointed_party .

iso:rel_186 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "REUSES the Part 3 node. The normative definition lives in ISO 19650-2, 3.1.3.4. Each task team shall establish and maintain a TIDP throughout its appointment, considering the project's information delivery milestones, the task team's responsibilities within the detailed responsibility matrix, the lead appointed party's information requirements, the availability of shared resources within the delivery team, and the time needed to generate, coordinate, review and approve information. The TIDP shall list and identify, for each information container: the name and title; the predecessors or dependencies; the level of information need; the (estimated) production duration; the information author responsible for its production; and the delivery milestones." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_tidp ;
    rdf:predicate iso:ESTABLISHES ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_task_team .

iso:rel_187 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_delivery_milestone ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_tidp .

iso:rel_188 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Each task team's TIDP shall consider the lead appointed party's information requirements. RESPONDS_TO is used as the traceability link; the clause also requires consideration of milestones, detailed responsibilities, shared-resource availability and production time." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_eir_iso19650_2 ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_tidp .

iso:rel_189 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.1.3.4; 5.4.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "A TIDP is a schedule of information containers and delivery dates for one task team; it lists and identifies required scheduling and responsibility attributes for each information container." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_container ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_tidp .

iso:rel_19 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.2.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_actor ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUBTYPE_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_client .

iso:rel_190 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.1.3.3; 5.4.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "MIDP = plan incorporating all relevant task information delivery plans (3.1.3.3)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_midp ;
    rdf:predicate iso:AGGREGATED_INTO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_tidp .

iso:rel_191 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "REUSES the Part 3 node. The normative definition lives in ISO 19650-2, 3.1.3.3. Established by aggregating the TIDP from each task team, considering the assigned responsibilities within the detailed responsibility matrix, information predecessors or dependencies between task teams, the time the lead appointed party will need to review and authorize the information model, and the time the appointing party will need to review and accept it. Once established, the lead appointed party shall baseline the deliverables and dates within the MIDP, inform each task team and notify any required TIDP changes, and inform the appointing party of any risks or issues which could impact the project's information delivery milestones." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_midp ;
    rdf:predicate iso:ESTABLISHES ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_lead_appointed_party .

iso:rel_192 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.6; 5.4.7" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The appointment activity completes the lead appointed party's and each appointed party's appointment documents, which are managed via change control throughout the duration of the appointment." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_appointment ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESULTS_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_appointment_delivery .

iso:rel_193 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.6; 5.4.7" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The appointing party's EIR are included within the lead appointed party's appointment documents (5.4.6); the lead appointed party's EIR are included within each appointed party's appointment documents (5.4.7)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_appointment ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_eir_iso19650_2 .

iso:rel_194 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.6; 5.4.7" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Including any agreed additions or amendments; managed via change control." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_appointment ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information_standard .

iso:rel_195 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.1.8; 5.4.6; 5.4.7" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Including any agreed additions or amendments; the protocol is incorporated into ALL appointments (5.1.8)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_appointment ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information_protocol .

iso:rel_196 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.6; 5.4.7" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_appointment ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_bim_execution_plan .

iso:rel_197 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.6" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Lead appointed party's appointment documents include the delivery team's MIDP." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_appointment ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_midp .

iso:rel_198 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.7" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Appointed party's appointment documents include the agreed TIDP." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_appointment ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_tidp .

iso:rel_199 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.5.1; 5.5.2; 5.5.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_mobilization_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONSIBLE_FOR ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_lead_appointed_party .

iso:rel_2 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.3.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_requirement ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUBTYPE_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_air .

iso:rel_20 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.2.3 Note 1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_appointed_party ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUBTYPE_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_lead_appointed_party .

iso:rel_200 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.5.1; 5.5.2; 5.5.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Resources, information technology and testing of the project's information production methods and procedures are all mobilized 'as defined within the delivery team's mobilization plan (5.3.5)'." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_mobilization_plan ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SPECIFIED_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_mobilization_delivery .

iso:rel_201 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.5.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Configure and test the project's CDE per 5.1.7, and configure and test the delivery team's (distributed) CDE and its connectivity to the project CDE (if applicable); test the information exchanges between task teams and the information delivery to the appointing party." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_cde ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_mobilization_delivery .

iso:rel_202 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.5.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Refine and verify that the proposed information container breakdown structure is workable." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_container_breakdown_structure ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_mobilization_delivery .

iso:rel_203 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.5.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Test and document the project's information production methods and procedures, develop shared resources to be used by the delivery team, and communicate the methods and procedures to all task teams." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_project_information_production_methods_procedures ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_mobilization_delivery .

iso:rel_204 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.6.1; 5.6.2; 5.6.3; 5.6.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Prior to generating information each task team shall check it has access to the relevant reference information and shared resources within the project's CDE and, if not, inform the lead appointed party as soon as practicable and assess the potential impact on the TIDP (5.6.1). Information model review (5.6.5) is undertaken by the delivery team as a whole." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_collaborative_production_of_information_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONSIBLE_FOR ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_task_team .

iso:rel_205 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.6.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Each task team shall generate information in accordance with their respective TIDP, in compliance with the project's information standard and in accordance with the project's information production methods and procedures." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_tidp ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SPECIFIED_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_collaborative_production_of_information_delivery .

iso:rel_206 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.6.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Relevant reference information and shared resources in the project's CDE are an explicit prerequisite to information generation; if unavailable, the task team shall notify the lead appointed party and assess the TIDP impact." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_collaborative_production_of_information_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_reference_information_shared_resources .

iso:rel_207 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.6.2 a); 5.6.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Generated information and information-container QA checks shall comply with the project's information standard." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_collaborative_production_of_information_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:GOVERNS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information_standard .

iso:rel_208 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.6.2-5.6.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Information generation, coordination, QA, review for sharing and information-model review are undertaken in accordance with the project's information production methods and procedures." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_collaborative_production_of_information_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:GOVERNS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information_production_methods_procedures .

iso:rel_209 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.6.3-5.6.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The reused root concept covers the distinct checks in this activity: information-container QA, review and approval for sharing, and delivery-team information-model review. A compliance check is not a substitute for review and approval." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_collaborative_production_of_information_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_information_verification_validation .

iso:rel_21 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.2.4; 6.3.2; Figure 6" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "the appointing party receives information from a lead appointed party; requirements are cascaded to the delivery team at key decision points" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_lead_appointed_party ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPOINTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_appointing_party .

iso:rel_210 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4; Figure 3 (A); 5.6; Figure 9" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The task-team production loops generate, coordinate, check and approve the information containers that progressively form the delivery-phase information model. CONTRIBUTES_TO is used because the activity progresses the PIM but does not by itself constitute final acceptance." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_pim ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CONTRIBUTES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_collaborative_production_of_information_delivery .

iso:rel_211 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.6.2 c); 5.6.2 d)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Task teams shall coordinate and cross-reference all information with information shared within the project's CDE, and spatially coordinate geometrical models with other geometrical models shared with the appropriate suitability. In the event of a coordination issue the relevant task teams shall collaborate to identify a possible resolution; if none can be found they shall notify the lead appointed party. PdM relevance: ISO 19650-1:2018, 11.1 classifies a 'soft clash' as one item occupying the operating or maintenance space of another." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_spatial_coordination_issue ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_collaborative_production_of_information_delivery .

iso:rel_212 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.6.2 b); 5.6.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Task teams shall not generate information that exceeds the required level of information need, extends beyond the allocated element of the information container breakdown structure, duplicates information generated by other task teams, or contains superfluous detail; level of information need is also a consideration of the review before sharing (5.6.4)." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_collaborative_production_of_information_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:GOVERNS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_level_of_information_need .

iso:rel_213 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.6.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "REUSES the Part 3 node. Each task team shall undertake a quality assurance check of each information container prior to undertaking a review of the information within it (5.6.4). If successful: mark the container as checked and record the outcome. If unsuccessful: reject the container and inform the information author of the outcome and corrective action required. NOTE 1: checks could be automated within the project's CDE. NOTE 2: a compliance check does not check the accuracy or appropriateness of the information within the container and cannot be seen as a replacement for review and approval (5.6.4)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_container ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_quality_assurance_check .

iso:rel_214 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.6.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The check is undertaken in accordance with the project's information production methods and procedures, and the container is checked in accordance with the project's information standard." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_project_information_production_methods_procedures ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SPECIFIED_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_quality_assurance_check .

iso:rel_215 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.6.3; 5.6.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Each task team shall review the information within the information container prior to sharing within the project's CDE, considering the lead appointed party's information requirements, the level of information need, and information needed for coordination by other task teams. If successful: assign the suitability for which the information can be used and approve the container for sharing. If unsuccessful: record why the review was unsuccessful, record any amendments for the task team to complete, and reject the container. UK National Annex NA.4.2 codifies the shared (non-contractual) suitabilities S1 (coordination within a delivery team), S2 (information/reference by other task teams), S3 (review and comment within a delivery team), S4 (review and authorization by a lead appointed party), S5 (review and acceptance by an appointing party); work in progress uses S0 with revision P01.01 upward (NA.4.3)." ;
    rdf:object iso:state_shared ;
    rdf:predicate iso:TRANSITIONS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:state_work_in_progress .

iso:rel_216 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.7.1; 5.7.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Each task team submits its information for lead appointed party authorization within the project's CDE (5.7.1). The lead appointed party reviews the information model in accordance with the project's information production methods and procedures, considering the deliverables listed in the MIDP, the appointing party's EIR, the lead appointed party's EIR, the acceptance criteria for each information requirement, and the level of information need for each information requirement. If successful it authorizes the model and instructs each task team to submit for appointing party acceptance; if unsuccessful it rejects the model and instructs task teams to amend and re-submit." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_information_model_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONSIBLE_FOR ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_lead_appointed_party .

iso:rel_217 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.7.3; 5.7.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The appointing party reviews the information model in accordance with the project's information production methods and procedures, considering the deliverables listed in the MIDP, the appointing party's EIR, the acceptance criteria for each information requirement, and the level of information need for each information requirement. If successful it accepts the model as a deliverable within the project's CDE; if unsuccessful it rejects the model and instructs the lead appointed party to amend and re-submit." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_information_model_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONSIBLE_FOR ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_appointing_party .

iso:rel_218 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.7.1-5.7.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Task-team submission, lead-appointed-party authorization and appointing-party acceptance all occur within the project's CDE." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_information_model_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_cde .

iso:rel_219 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.7.2; 5.7.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Both authorization and acceptance reviews shall be undertaken in accordance with the project's information production methods and procedures." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_information_model_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:GOVERNS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information_production_methods_procedures .

iso:rel_22 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.3; 5.5; 6.3.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "EIR/AIR received by a lead appointed party can be sub-divided and passed on in any of its own appointments, and so on along the supply chain" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_appointed_party ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPOINTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_lead_appointed_party .

iso:rel_220 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.7.2; 5.7.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The authorization review considers both appointing-party and lead-appointed-party EIR; the acceptance review considers the appointing-party EIR. GOVERNS is a traceability shorthand for these required review inputs." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_information_model_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:GOVERNS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_eir_iso19650_2 .

iso:rel_221 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.7.2; 5.7.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Both authorization and acceptance reviews consider the level of information need for each information requirement." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_information_model_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:GOVERNS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_level_of_information_need .

iso:rel_222 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Figure 1; 5.7.1-5.7.4; 5.8.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Successful authorization and appointing-party acceptance produce the accepted delivery-phase information model referred to as the completed PIM at project close-out. Rejected models loop back for amendment and re-submission." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_pim ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESULTS_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_information_model_delivery .

iso:rel_223 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.7.2; 5.7.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_information_model_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:GOVERNS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_acceptance_criteria .

iso:rel_224 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.7.2; 5.7.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Both the authorization and acceptance reviews consider the deliverables listed in the MIDP; partial acceptance of the information to be exchanged as defined within the MIDP can lead to coordination issues, so the whole model should be authorized/accepted or rejected." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_information_model_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:GOVERNS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_midp .

iso:rel_225 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.7.2; 5.7.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "ISO 19650-2 operationalizes the ISO 19650-1:2018, 6.3.3 concept into two checking loops: lead appointed party authorization (5.7.2) and appointing party acceptance (5.7.4). No new node is created for 'information model review'." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_information_model_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_information_verification_validation .

iso:rel_226 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.7.2; 5.7.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Two-step gate: lead appointed party authorization (5.7.2) then appointing party acceptance (5.7.4), after which the information model is accepted as a deliverable within the project's CDE. UK National Annex NA.4.2 codifies the published (contractual) status as A1, An etc. with contractual revision C01 upward (NA.4.3); B1, Bn (partially signed off with comments) is marked DEPRECATED in the 2021 corrigendum, consistent with 5.7.2/5.7.4 discouraging partial acceptance." ;
    rdf:object iso:state_published ;
    rdf:predicate iso:TRANSITIONS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:state_shared .

iso:rel_227 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8.1; 5.8.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Archiving is the appointing party's responsibility; lessons learned are captured by the appointing party in collaboration with each lead appointed party." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_project_close_out_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONSIBLE_FOR ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_appointing_party .

iso:rel_228 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Upon acceptance of the completed PIM, its information containers are archived within the project's CDE." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_project_close_out_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_cde .

iso:rel_229 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_project_close_out_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information_model_archive .

iso:rel_23 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.2.3 Note 1; 3.2.6" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "a lead appointed party should be identified for each delivery team" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_delivery_team ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LEADS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_lead_appointed_party .

iso:rel_230 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Undertaken upon acceptance of the COMPLETED project information model." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_pim ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information_model_archive .

iso:rel_231 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: ISO 19650-2, 5.8.1 requires archiving information containers within the project's CDE but does not name the Part 1 archive-state ontology. This relationship aligns the action to ISO 19650-1:2018, 12.7, where the archive state is the journal of shared/published containers and their development audit trail." ;
    rdf:object iso:state_archive ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CORRESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information_model_archive .

iso:rel_232 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE ONTOLOGY ALIGNMENT: 5.8.1 directly requires the completed PIM's information containers to be archived within the CDE. RECORDED_IN maps that requirement to the Part 1 archive-state concept without implying that the entire PIM transitions out of its current state or that every PIM container becomes part of the AIM." ;
    rdf:object iso:state_archive ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RECORDED_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_pim .

iso:rel_233 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Archiving is undertaken in accordance with the project's information production methods and procedures." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_project_information_production_methods_procedures ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SPECIFIED_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information_model_archive .

iso:rel_234 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: when archiving the PIM, the appointing party shall consider 'which information containers will be needed as part of the asset information model', together with future access requirements, future re-use and relevant retention policies. This is the normative decision point that determines which data survives into the operational phase and is therefore available for PdM analytics." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_aim ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information_model_archive .

iso:rel_235 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: ISO 19650-2, 5.8.1 does not name AIR in the archive decision. The link follows ISO 19650-1:2018, 3.3.4 and 5.3, where AIR specifies the AIM, and ISO 19650-3:2020, 5.1.12, where information is verified against AIR when maintaining the AIM." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_air ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information_model_archive .

iso:rel_236 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: 5.8.1 does not name the purpose; the link is derived via ISO 19650-1:2018, 5.1 (the purpose 'maintenance and repair' - information on the recommended maintenance tasks including planned preventative maintenance) and 5.7 (the PIM's contents include details of installed systems, components and equipment including maintenance requirements)." ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_maintenance_repair ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information_model_archive .

iso:rel_237 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "0.1; Figure 1 (C); 5.8.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "THE CENTRAL PdM HANDOVER POINT. Figure 1 key C: 'end of delivery phase - transfer of relevant information from PIM to AIM'. The normative requirement realizing point C sits at 5.8.1: when archiving the project information model, the appointing party shall consider which information containers will be needed as part of the AIM. CONTRIBUTES_TO therefore represents selective transfer of relevant containers, not aggregation of the entire PIM. This duplicates the corrected (from, type, to) triple of ISO 19650-1 (5.7; 12.1; Figure 2; Figure 3 point C) - deliberately kept separate because provenance differs; when loading into Neo4j, MERGE on (from, type, to) and collect provenance into an array. CORRECTION relative to the original task brief: this is point C, not point B." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_aim ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CONTRIBUTES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_pim .

iso:rel_238 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "0.1; Figure 1 (A)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Figure 1 key A: 'start of delivery phase - transfer of relevant information from AIM to PIM'. The reverse direction of the information loop: the AIM of an existing asset is the source of the 'existing asset information' that 5.1.5 a) and 5.1.6 a) require to be captured. This duplicates the (from, type, to) triple of an ISO 19650-1 relationship (5.6; 4.1; Figure 3 point A) - handle by MERGE as above." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_pim ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CONTRIBUTES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_aim .

iso:rel_239 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "0.1; Figure 1 (B)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_pim ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_design_intent_model .

iso:rel_24 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.2.6" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "delivery team = lead appointed party and their appointed parties" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_delivery_team ;
    rdf:predicate iso:MEMBER_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_appointed_party .

iso:rel_240 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "0.1; Figure 1 (B)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_pim ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_virtual_construction_model .

iso:rel_241 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "0.1; Figure 1 (B)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Figure 1 key B: 'progressive development of the design intent model into the virtual construction model'." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_virtual_construction_model ;
    rdf:predicate iso:DEVELOPED_INTO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_design_intent_model .

iso:rel_242 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "0.1; Figure 1 (B, C)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: Figure 1 directly states point B (design intent model progressively developed into the virtual construction model) and point C (transfer of relevant information from PIM to AIM), but it does not state that the virtual construction model is an as-built record or that all of it transfers. This edge preserves the inferred path only for selected, relevant PIM content." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_aim ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CONTRIBUTES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_virtual_construction_model .

iso:rel_243 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "0.1; Figure 1 (C); 5.2.1 a)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: ISO 19650-2 does not state directly that the virtual construction model answers the AIR. The link is inferred from 5.2.1 a) (EIR shall consider AIR), ISO 19650-1 Figure 2 (EIR specifies PIM), and Figure 1 point C. It represents a requirements-traceability question about which installed-asset information must be delivered, not a normative definition of virtual construction model content." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_air ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_virtual_construction_model .

iso:rel_244 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "0.1; Figure 1 (B, C)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: derived via ISO 19650-1:2018, 5.7 (the PIM contains details of installed systems, components and equipment including maintenance requirements) and the 5.1 purpose 'maintenance and repair'." ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_maintenance_repair ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_virtual_construction_model .

iso:rel_245 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "0.1; Figure 1 (B, C)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: derived via ISO 19650-1:2018, 5.7 and the 5.1 purpose 'operations'." ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_operations ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_virtual_construction_model .

iso:rel_246 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_project_close_out_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_lessons_learned .

iso:rel_247 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "In collaboration with each lead appointed party; recorded in a suitable knowledge store to be called upon by future projects." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_lessons_learned ;
    rdf:predicate iso:ESTABLISHES ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_appointing_party .

iso:rel_248 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: 5.8.2 directly requires lessons to be captured and recorded for future projects. Relating that knowledge store to the broader information-management concept and continual-improvement principle uses ISO 19650-1:2018, 6.2 and its ISO 9001 context." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_management ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_lessons_learned .

iso:rel_249 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.8.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-2" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: bridges the PdM feedback loop across the two phases. ISO 19650-2, 5.8.2 captures project lessons into a knowledge store for future projects; ISO 19650-3, A.3 defines the trigger 'performance evaluation of an asset' as including failure trends from similar components used elsewhere and experience-based learning and feedback from asset performance. These are the two ends of the same learning loop, but neither standard connects them explicitly." ;
    rdf:object iso:trigger_performance_evaluation ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_lessons_learned .

iso:rel_25 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.2.6 Note 3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "a delivery team can consist of multiple task teams from within the lead appointed party's organization and any appointed parties" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_delivery_team ;
    rdf:predicate iso:MEMBER_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_task_team .

iso:rel_250 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.2; 5.8.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-3" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: the process interface between the two Parts. The output of ISO 19650-2, 5.8.1 (the information containers identified as needed for the AIM) is the input to ISO 19650-3, 5.8.1 (the appointing party incorporates an accepted information model into its AIM and reconciles it with existing AIM contents). Neither standard connects these two activities explicitly; the link is inferred from ISO 19650-3, 4.2 (where both standards apply, responsibilities shall be established and communicated between the two appointing parties) and from point C of Figure 1 / Figure 3." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_aim_aggregation ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:activity_project_close_out_delivery .

iso:rel_251 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-3" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "BRIDGE BETWEEN THE TWO EIR BRANCHES. ISO 19650-3:2020, 4.2: where both ISO 19650-2 and ISO 19650-3 apply, the EIR of the ISO 19650-3 appointing party are specified to the lead appointed parties appointed under ISO 19650-2. Both nodes REFINE term_eir but do not replace one another: the operational branch feeds requirements into the delivery branch." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_eir_iso19650_2 ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CONTRIBUTES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_eir_iso19650_3 .

iso:rel_252 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-3" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "BRIDGE BETWEEN THE TWO BRANCHES. ISO 19650-3:2020, 4.2 requires CONSISTENCY between the asset information standard and the project information standard where both standards apply. This is the mechanism ensuring that information produced during the project can be loaded into the AIM without re-mapping - a precondition for any PdM data pipeline." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_information_standard ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information_standard .

iso:rel_253 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-3" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "BRIDGE BETWEEN THE TWO BRANCHES. ISO 19650-3:2020, 4.2 requires CONSISTENCY between the asset and project information production methods and procedures where both standards apply." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_information_production_methods_procedures ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information_production_methods_procedures .

iso:rel_254 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "0.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-3" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Two distinct management disciplines with their own standards and preferred terms; for simplicity the main body of ISO 19650-3 uses 'asset management' to cover both." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_management ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CORRESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_facility_management .

iso:rel_255 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "0.2; 1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-3" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Asset management and facility management activities delivered during the operational phase of an asset." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_operational_phase ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_asset_management .

iso:rel_256 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "A.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-3" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "A wide range of organizational activities, including asset management and facility management activities, can lead to the OIR; grouping activities as strategic/tactical/operational helps identify frequency of information need and stakeholder types." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_management ;
    rdf:predicate iso:DERIVED_FROM ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_oir .

iso:rel_257 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-3" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Applied throughout the operational phase of each asset identified through 5.1.3." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_operational_phase ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_im_process_operational .

iso:rel_258 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-3" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "For an existing asset the process shall be applied to all legacy information relating to that asset." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_legacy_information ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_im_process_operational .

iso:rel_259 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "0.1; Figure 4 (H)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-3" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Process can be applied to foreseen trigger events and to unforeseen/unscheduled trigger events; decision point H = type of trigger event providing information." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_trigger_event ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_im_process_operational .

iso:rel_26 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "12.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "compares the information container against the information delivery plan and against the agreed standards, methods and procedures; made by the originating task team" ;
    rdf:object iso:state_shared ;
    rdf:predicate iso:TRANSITIONS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:state_work_in_progress .

iso:rel_260 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "0.1; 5.1.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-3" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_trigger_event ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUBTYPE_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_foreseen_trigger_event .

iso:rel_261 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "0.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-3" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_trigger_event ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUBTYPE_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_unforeseen_trigger_event .

