iso:rel_673 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "8.4.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-5" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The assessment shall examine the causes of the event, identify potential countermeasures, and assess the residual risk as well as any potential new or exacerbated risk arising from the event." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_residual_risk ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_post_incident_review .

iso:rel_674 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "8.4.2; 7.6.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-5" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The relevant policies and processes shall be updated to reflect the findings and to prevent or reduce the risk of a re-occurrence." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_security_management_plan ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_post_incident_review .

iso:rel_675 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "9.1.1; 9.1.2; D.1.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-5" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Required when working OUTSIDE formal appointments (for example during tendering) if access is to be granted to sensitive information; shall include the organization's requirements for the retention, disposal and destruction of sensitive information." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_sensitive_information ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_information_sharing_agreement .

iso:rel_676 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "D.1.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-5" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Informative (Annex D): information sharing agreements should be reviewed at the frequency DEFINED IN the security management plan, to establish the effectiveness of the sharing and to confirm that there is still a legitimate purpose for continued sharing with each recipient (and that access has been withdrawn where there is not), that information quality and maintenance meet the agreed standards, and that the information security arrangements remain appropriate and proportionate." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_security_management_plan ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SPECIFIED_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_information_sharing_agreement .

iso:rel_677 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "D.1.2 d); D.1.4 b)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-5" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Informative Annex D.1.2 d) recommends that an agreement state the authenticity, coverage, accuracy, relevance and usability of shared information. This is a useful place to agree measurable PdM data-quality expectations, while the normative obligation to use an agreement outside formal appointments comes from 9.1.1-9.1.2." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_quality ;
    rdf:predicate iso:GOVERNS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_information_sharing_agreement .

iso:rel_678 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "7.1.4; 9.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-5" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "7.1.4: the security management plan shall be used to inform the security requirements embedded into any procurement and appointment documents. 9.2.1: the organization shall manage its delivery team security risks through provisions in the appointment documentation supporting all relevant security policies and processes in the plan, INCLUDING the requirements placed on a delivery team member at the END of an appointment. 9.2.2: the allocation of the information security function to the delivery team shall be detailed, including the requirement for security to be retained at accountable levels within the delivery team with responsibility delegated appropriately. 9.2.3: where appropriate the provisions shall be applied through the layers of sub-appointments. 9.2.4: where compliance with specific security standards is required, this shall be clearly identified in the appointment documentation along with any expected independent third-party inspection or verification. 9.2.6: provisions shall allow the organization to review security measures and compliance at ANY level in the delivery team. 9.2.7: a clause shall be inserted enabling adjustments in response to changes in the political, legislative or regulatory environment. 9.3.1: after award, all security-related provisions shall be monitored and enforced. 9.3.2: the organization shall work with its delivery team to assist understanding of the security requirements and to address any outstanding security issues." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_appointment ;
    rdf:predicate iso:GOVERNS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_security_management_plan .

iso:rel_679 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "7.1.3 a)-b)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-5" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_security_management_plan ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_security_policy_process .

