    iso:provenanceClause "4.2; Figure 1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "information management can be represented as a sequence of maturity stages; standards development, technology advances and more sophisticated information management combine to deliver increasing business benefit" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_management ;
    rdf:predicate iso:STAGE_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_maturity_stage_3 .

iso:rel_850 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.3; Table 2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: demolition falls outside both the delivery phase and the operational phase as ISO 19650-1 defines them, so it is linked directly to the life cycle (3.2.10: from the definition of requirements to the termination of use, covering disposal). Compare trigger_end_of_life_works of ISO 19650-3, A.3 and purpose_decommissioning_disposal of ISO 19650-1, 5.1." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_life_cycle ;
    rdf:predicate iso:STAGE_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:stage_demolition .

iso:rel_851 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.3; Table 2; 5.4.3 c) 3)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: risks and incidents carrying Application stage = Operation are the set of records bearing directly on maintenance and repair; 5.4.3 c) 3) explicitly requires information to enable the SAFE repair, maintenance or replacement of plant and equipment." ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_maintenance_repair ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SERVES_PURPOSE ;
    rdf:subject iso:stage_operation .

iso:rel_852 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.3; Table 2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE." ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_decommissioning_disposal ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SERVES_PURPOSE ;
    rdf:subject iso:stage_demolition .

iso:rel_853 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.3; Table 2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: the 'support for renovation' purpose of ISO 19650-1, 5.1 requires detailed information about capacity in terms of areas, spaces, occupancy, environmental conditions and structural load bearing." ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_renovation ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SERVES_PURPOSE ;
    rdf:subject iso:stage_repurposing .

iso:rel_854 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Introduction; 4.5.5 b)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK. Introduction: during handover and close out of the project, the health and safety information is used TO ENSURE THAT THE PROJECT INFORMATION MODEL IS USED TO UPDATE THE ASSET INFORMATION MODEL, and this information is handed over to those who will be responsible for managing and assessing health and safety risks during the operational phase. 4.5.5 b) requires generalization at any close out stage. This is the SPECIFIC reason for the PIM-to-AIM transfer that ISO 19650-2, 5.8.1 states only generically ('which information containers will be needed as part of the asset information model')." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_project_close_out_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CORRESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:stage_handover .

iso:rel_855 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex C; Table C.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Informative (Annex C): likelihood and consequence CAN be added to Tables 2 and 3 to be encoded using a five-level textual enumeration." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_level_of_risk ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_likelihood .

iso:rel_856 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex C; Table C.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_level_of_risk ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_consequence .

iso:rel_857 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex C; Table C.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Informative (Annex C): the level of risk can be derived from likelihood and consequence using the 5x5 combination matrix of Table C.2." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_level_of_risk ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SPECIFIED_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_risk_level_matrix .

iso:rel_858 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex C; Table C.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_risk_level_matrix ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_likelihood .

iso:rel_859 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex C; Table C.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_risk_level_matrix ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_consequence .

iso:rel_86 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Stage 2 maturity is identified as 'BIM according to the ISO 19650 series'" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_bim ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CORRESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_maturity_stage_2 .

iso:rel_860 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex C; Table C.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "A VERY STRONG PdM HOOK: Table C.3 maps the five levels of risk onto five levels of operational priority - very urgent / urgent / short term / medium term / long term." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_level_of_risk ;
    rdf:predicate iso:DERIVED_FROM ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_risk_urgency_prioritization .

iso:rel_861 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex C; Table C.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive but almost direct. Table C.3 states for each level that it 'can relate to X prioritization DURING OPERATIONS' - the language of maintenance scheduling. Table C.2 combined with Table C.3 yields a complete decision rule: a prediction model output expressed as likelihood x consequence falls automatically into one of the five urgency levels without a scale of its own." ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_maintenance_repair ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_risk_urgency_prioritization .

iso:rel_862 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex C; Table C.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive. Consequence is the quantity a prediction model cannot infer from sensor data - it has to come from the AIM. term_asset_criticality (ISO 19650-3, 5.1.3 and A.4.4: the criticality of assets and spaces to the organization) is the direct data source for grading consequence." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_criticality ;
    rdf:predicate iso:DERIVED_FROM ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_consequence .

iso:rel_863 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex C; Table C.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive. term_downtime_impact (ISO 19650-3, A.4.5 and A.2: the operational and financial impact of asset unavailability or failure) is the quantitative source for the consequence grade, especially for the Substantial impact and Catastrophic consequences levels of Table C.3." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_downtime_impact ;
    rdf:predicate iso:DERIVED_FROM ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_consequence .

iso:rel_864 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex C; Table C.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "A CORE PdM HOOK: interpretive. term_asset_performance_prediction is the only predictive example OIR in the entire series (ISO 19650-3, A.2: information to support a means to predict the performance of the asset). Likelihood is exactly the quantity a prediction model estimates. Implementation recommendation: quantize the model output onto the five-level scale of Table C.1 so that it slots straight into the Likelihood field of Table 2 without a separate mapping layer - Annex C records that fewer or more than five levels are less effective for communication." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_performance_prediction ;
    rdf:predicate iso:DERIVED_FROM ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_likelihood .

iso:rel_865 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.5; Table 4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive. Both scheduled preventive maintenance and condition-based maintenance are engineering controls under the Table 4 classification - meaning a predictive maintenance programme can be REGISTERED as a risk treatment in the schema, linked to the specific risks it addresses, with an Approved by, a Review date, and a before/after risk level pair evidencing its effectiveness." ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_maintenance_repair ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SERVES_PURPOSE ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_treatment_control .

iso:rel_866 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.2 Note 1; Table 4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive. Note 1 to 3.2 lists INFORMING as one of four ways a risk can be modified. A failure-prediction alert sent to a maintenance team is a risk treatment of category Information - so the output of a PdM system has a formal place in the Table 4 schema without needing a new concept." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_performance_prediction ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_treatment_information .

iso:rel_867 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.6" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The properties requirements necessary FOR health and safety information to be usable shall be documented THROUGHOUT THE ASSET LIFE CYCLE." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_health_safety_information ;
    rdf:predicate iso:ENABLES ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_properties .

iso:rel_868 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.6 NOTE" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "THE STRONGEST PdM HOOK IN PART 6: properties linked to geometric and construction and operation sequencing models enable engineering analysis, support judgements on risk factors such as DEFLECTION LIMITS and LOAD CAPACITIES, and 'ENABLE ACTIVE NEAR-REAL-TIME DIGITAL MONITORING TECHNIQUES'." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_construction_operation_sequencing_model ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_properties .

iso:rel_869 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.6 NOTE" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive. The phrase 'active near-real-time digital monitoring techniques' in the NOTE to 4.3.6 describes exactly the function ISO 19650-3, A.5 calls a condition monitoring system. The added value: Part 6 ties it to specific STRUCTURAL ENGINEERING quantities (deflection limits, load capacities), i.e. measurable condition indicators rather than generic operational data." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_condition_monitoring_system ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_properties .

iso:rel_87 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "11.3; 11.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "information managed in the CDE should be understandable by all parties; security and information quality should be considered and integrated into the definition of or proposals for the CDE (11.1)" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_cde ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_information_quality .

iso:rel_870 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.6 NOTE" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: deflection limits and load capacities are quantities describing the condition and duty of an asset in the sense of ISO 19650-3, A.4.4." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_condition_duty ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_properties .

iso:rel_871 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.6; 4.5.2 d)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "4.5.2 d): each party shall expand, populate and utilize the properties WITHIN THE RELEVANT INFORMATION CONTAINERS to treat, manage and communicate prioritized health and safety risks, risk treatments and incidents." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_container ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_properties .

iso:rel_872 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.3 b); 6.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_model ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUBTYPE_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_construction_operation_sequencing_model .

iso:rel_873 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.3 b)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: the two model types are complementary. term_virtual_construction_model (ISO 19650-2, Figure 1 point B) describes the as-built STATE; the construction and operation sequencing model describes the SEQUENCE over time and is the only model type in the series with an explicit operation dimension in its name." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_virtual_construction_model ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CORRESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_construction_operation_sequencing_model .

iso:rel_874 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "A CDE as described in ISO 19650-1 SHALL be created and used to host and manage the health and safety register and other information, and to share it between the members of the project team (ISO 19650-2) or of the asset/facility management and operation team (ISO 19650-3)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_cde ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_information_sharing .

iso:rel_875 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_cde ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_register .

iso:rel_876 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3; 4.5.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The register is the living record-store embodiment of the Table 1-4 schema." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_schema ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SPECIFIED_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_register .

iso:rel_877 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.2; 5.1 NOTE" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Counterpart but NOT identical: term_risk_register (ISO 19650-3, 5.3.6) is the delivery team's register of risks to the PRODUCTION AND DELIVERY OF INFORMATION; the health and safety register is a register of risks to PEOPLE AND ASSETS. The two nodes are kept separate. The NOTE to 5.1 permits shared access to the risk register as a way of gathering contributions from multiple parties." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_risk_register ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CORRESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_register .

iso:rel_878 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.2.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_schema ;
    rdf:predicate iso:ESTABLISHES ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_appointing_party .

iso:rel_879 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Appointing parties, lead appointed parties AND appointed parties shall all share ALL generated health and safety information with ALL parties - the opposite of the chain-of-appointment default in the other Parts, because the Introduction treats this as a collective responsibility." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_information_sharing ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONSIBLE_FOR ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_appointed_party .

iso:rel_88 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "11.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "issues in the information model should be avoided during the production of information rather than detected after delivery" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_model ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_spatial_coordination_issue .

iso:rel_880 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.2; 4.5.4; 6.6" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The lead appointed party shall consider the need to share with OTHER LEAD APPOINTED PARTIES in order to manage project risks effectively, whether the appointments are concurrent or in parallel (4.5.2); shall coordinate the USE of the risk information (4.5.4); and shall coordinate the PRODUCTION of health and safety information by its delivery team with any other active delivery teams (6.6)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_information_sharing ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONSIBLE_FOR ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_lead_appointed_party .

iso:rel_881 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM TENSION AND ITS RECONCILIATION MECHANISM. The 'share everything with everyone' default of 4.5.2 collides head-on with the need-to-know principle (ISO 19650-5, 3.4) and the mandatory pre-sharing assessment (7.2). 4.5.5 states the reconciliation mechanism explicitly: the appointing party shall ensure health and safety information is available throughout the life cycle and used for planning, training, inductions and risk awareness, 'WHILST REMAINING SECURITY-MINDED'." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_security_minded_approach ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_information_sharing .

iso:rel_882 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.3; 4.5.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "THE RECONCILIATION MECHANISM WITH PART 5: generalization is the act of removing or modifying details to make information suitable for wider publication and re-use, which can include replacing personal and protected characteristics. It is how LESSONS can be shared without disseminating sensitive information. Functionally the counterpart of term_information_redaction in ISO 19650-5, C.2.2, but with the opposite motive: redaction protects, generalization disseminates." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_information_sharing ;
    rdf:predicate iso:ENABLES ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_generalization .

iso:rel_883 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.3 Note 1; 4.5.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Note 1 to 3.3: this can include replacing personal and protected characteristics. Footnote b to Table A.1: organizational, project or role based identification can be used in preference to personal identification in the Affected party, Raised by, Owned by and Approved by fields." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_sensitive_information ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_generalization .

iso:rel_884 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.5; 5.4.5 b)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "REUSES the Part 2 node. Each party shall release GENERALIZED information on lessons learned, innovation and improved practices associated with health and safety risk management for continued learning through their management system arrangements. This supplies the motive and mechanism for term_lessons_learned, which ISO 19650-2, 5.8.2 states only as 'record them in a suitable knowledge store'." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_lessons_learned ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESULTS_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_generalization .

iso:rel_885 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_generalization ;
    rdf:predicate iso:DERIVED_FROM ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_reusable_hs_information .

iso:rel_886 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.5 b)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_lessons_learned ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_reusable_hs_information .

iso:rel_887 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.5 NOTE; 5.4.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive. NOTE to 4.5.5: documenting all known or perceived health and safety risks helps to provide A LEARNING PLATFORM for other members of the industry, capturing tacit knowledge for sharing amongst a wider community. This is the normative mechanism for data to cross organizational boundaries - the precondition for having enough training samples for equipment types that rarely fail, and the counterpart of 'failure trends from similar components used ELSEWHERE' in trigger_performance_evaluation (ISO 19650-3, A.3)." ;
    rdf:object iso:trigger_performance_evaluation ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_reusable_hs_information .

iso:rel_888 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Introduction" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: 'One important use of incident information is to link incidents to design factors, so that designers can learn about how their designed assets perform in use.'" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_incident ;
    rdf:predicate iso:DERIVED_FROM ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_design_factor_learning .

iso:rel_889 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Introduction" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    rdf:object iso:stage_design ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_design_factor_learning .

iso:rel_89 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "11.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "the clash-avoidance principle reinforces the requirement for a federation strategy" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_spatial_coordination_issue ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_federation_strategy .

iso:rel_890 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Introduction" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive. term_asset_failure_history (ISO 19650-3, A.4.1: details of historical asset failures, causes and consequences if known) and the Part 6 incident schema record the same class of event for two different purposes: Part 3 in order to PREDICT, Part 6 in order to LEARN AND PREVENT. An equipment failure causing injury is simultaneously a record on both." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_failure_history ;
    rdf:predicate iso:CORRESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_design_factor_learning .

iso:rel_891 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Introduction" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive. Linking incidents to design factors is how operational failure data becomes design improvement for the next generation of assets, rather than merely optimizing the maintenance schedule of the current one - extending the scope of term_asset_performance_prediction (ISO 19650-3, A.2) from one asset to an asset class." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_performance_prediction ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_design_factor_learning .

iso:rel_892 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_risk ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_buildability_maintainability_review .

iso:rel_893 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Each appointed party shall review whether their proposals are BUILDABLE and MAINTAINABLE." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_buildability_maintainability_review ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONSIBLE_FOR ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_appointed_party .

iso:rel_894 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: the ONLY normative requirement in the entire ISO 19650 series obliging the designer or constructor to demonstrate that a proposal is MAINTAINABLE. It is the process-level counterpart of the soft clash concept (ISO 19650-1, 11.1: one item occupying the operating or maintenance space of another) and of the generic information rule (11.1: information shall indicate the space required for installation, connection, maintenance and replacement)." ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_maintenance_repair ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SERVES_PURPOSE ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_buildability_maintainability_review .

iso:rel_895 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: the 'soft clash' of ISO 19650-1, 11.1 is defined as one item occupying the operating or maintenance space of another - precisely the class of problem a maintainability review has to detect." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_spatial_coordination_issue ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONDS_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_buildability_maintainability_review .

iso:rel_896 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_risk_management_strategy ;
    rdf:predicate iso:ESTABLISHES ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_appointing_party .

iso:rel_897 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Each appointing party SHALL include health and safety requirements in the organizational information requirements, comprising an agreed information schema, the connections required to use the health and safety information WITH OTHER DATASETS, and the risk management strategy. Introduction: organizational information requirements developed by the appointing party can reflect the required integration of health and safety as well as modelling and sharing of information across the supply chain." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_oir ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_risk_management_strategy .

iso:rel_898 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.1 a)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The OIR shall include an agreed information schema capturing the categorization of health and safety information in accordance with 4.3." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_oir ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_schema .

iso:rel_899 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: an appointing party that owns and/or is responsible for assets SHALL include health and safety information requirements in the AIR a) to consider the regulatory health and safety requirements on the management or development of an asset, and b) TO ENSURE INFORMATION GENERATED IN A DELIVERY OR IN-USE PHASE IS AVAILABLE DURING SUBSEQUENT PHASES. Item b) is a cross-phase data continuity requirement, stronger than the wording of ISO 19650-2, 5.8.1. The appointing party shall also consider expected standards and the reporting of performance criteria." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_air ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_9 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.3; Figure 2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Figure 2: AIR 'specifies' (determines the content, structure and methodology of) AIM" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_air ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SPECIFIED_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_aim .

iso:rel_90 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "11.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "generic information used before final product selection indicates space for installation, connection, maintenance and replacement, and is replaced by specific information as soon as available" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_container ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_generic_information .

iso:rel_900 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "An appointing party initiating a delivery phase SHALL include health and safety information requirements in the PIR, meeting the risk and hazard profile of the delivery phase and setting out at a high level a framework for managing health and safety information throughout the delivery phase, from inception to completion and handover. The items to be considered: the purpose and objectives for the specified risk management tasks; collaborative risk studies, reviews and discussions between subject matter experts; the timing at which information is to be shared with external parties for regulative, approval or permit purposes; and the appointing party's internal processes including review points to assure that collaboration and exchange is effective." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_pir ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_901 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Each appointing party AND each lead appointed party shall incorporate health and safety information requirements into EACH set of exchange information requirements established for each relevant appointment." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_eir ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_902 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.1; 6.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The delivery-phase branch of the same 5.4.1 requirement, since 6.1 requires health and safety information to be managed in accordance with ISO 19650-2 or ISO 19650-3." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_eir_iso19650_2 ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_903 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.1; 6.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The operational-phase branch of the same 5.4.1 requirement." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_eir_iso19650_3 ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_904 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Evidence supporting the delivered information, including evidence of compliance with legislative obligations and duties." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_eir ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_supporting_evidence .

iso:rel_905 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.4 b)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "purpose_compliance_regulatory of ISO 19650-1, 5.1: the appointing party should specify the information required to support the maintenance of the health and safety of THE USERS of the asset. Part 6 is the full realization of that purpose." ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_compliance_regulatory ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SERVES_PURPOSE ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_supporting_evidence .

iso:rel_906 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.2 a); 5.4.4 b)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_compliance_regulatory ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SERVES_PURPOSE ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_907 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.2.1 a)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "purpose_risk_management of ISO 19650-1, 5.1: information should be required or suppressed to support risk management, especially to identify and review the risks that a project or asset can be exposed to." ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_risk_management ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SERVES_PURPOSE ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_908 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.3 c) 3)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: 5.4.3 c) 3) explicitly requires 'information to enable the SAFE REPAIR, MAINTENANCE OR REPLACEMENT of plant and equipment INCLUDING ASSUMPTIONS'. The words 'including assumptions' matter: they compel recording the assumptions underpinning a maintenance procedure, which is what is needed in order to know when that procedure ceases to be valid." ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_maintenance_repair ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SERVES_PURPOSE ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_909 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.3 c) 1)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "5.4.3 c) 1) requires information on construction and operation, maintenance and repurposing methods, constructability and OPERABILITY, and critical sequences." ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_operations ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SERVES_PURPOSE ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_91 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "8.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "review of the prospective delivery team's capability and capacity to meet the information requirements" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_delivery_team ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_capability_capacity_review .

iso:rel_910 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.3 c) 3)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: 5.4.3 c) 3) also names the 'replacement of plant and equipment'." ;
    rdf:object iso:purpose_replacement ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SERVES_PURPOSE ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_911 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.4.3 a) 2); 5.4.3 b) 2)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive. 5.4.3 a) 2) requires information on 'SAFETY CRITICAL zones, areas and spaces' and 5.4.3 b) 2) on 'SAFETY CRITICAL systems, fixed assets and equipment'. This is a THIRD criticality scale alongside business criticality (ISO 19650-3, 5.1.3 asset criticality) and security criticality (ISO 19650-5, 4.3.2 sensitive built asset). The three frequently coincide but are not identical; a PdM system should carry all three as separate asset attributes." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_criticality ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_912 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.1 b); 5.4.3 c)" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive. 5.1 b) requires the OIR to state the 'connections required to facilitate use of the health and safety information WITH OTHER DATASETS'. The maintenance history (ISO 19650-3, A.4.1) is the most directly related dataset: each maintenance task is both an activity with its own safety risk and evidence about the condition of the equipment." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_maintenance_history ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_913 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.1 b); 4.3.6 NOTE" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: the 'design limits' in term_asset_operational_data (ISO 19650-3, A.4.2) and the 'deflection limits, load capacities' in the NOTE to 4.3.6 are the same class of threshold quantity, approached from two axes." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_operational_data ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_914 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Health and safety information shall be recorded in the relevant information containers, using structured tables or databases, and/or by adding it into the geometric, construction and operation sequenced or work planning model, attached to physical, spatial and/or process entities or types, or to annotation entities in close proximity." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_container ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_information_presentation .

iso:rel_915 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The requirement to exchange and share in STRUCTURED, OPEN STANDARD (non-proprietary) forms is mandatory - stronger wording than the 'using open standards whenever possible' of principle 4 in ISO 19650-1, clause 6.1." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_quality ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_information_presentation .

iso:rel_916 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex D" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Informative (Annex D): a mapping of the 4.3 schema to ISO 16739-1 IFC4.3, IFC4.0 and IFC2x3." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_schema ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SPECIFIED_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_ifc_representation .

iso:rel_917 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex D; Table D.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: IFC4.3 separates the before/after value pair for all three quantities (UnmitigatedRiskLikelihood/MitigatedRiskLikelihood, UnmitigatedRiskConsequence/MitigatedRiskConsequence, UnmitigatedRiskSignificance/MitigatedRiskSignificance), implementing the twice-over assessment requirement of 4.2.4. IFC4.0 has single values only, and IFC2x3 has a simplified Pset_Risk with no IfcTaskType - losing the ability to attach a risk to a task type." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_risk_prioritization ;
    rdf:predicate iso:ENABLES ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_ifc_representation .

iso:rel_918 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex B" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Informative (Annex B)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_categorization ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_classification_health .

iso:rel_919 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex B" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Informative (Annex B)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_categorization ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_classification_welfare .

iso:rel_92 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "8.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "the review can be done by the appointing party, by the prospective delivery team themselves or by an independent party; scope made available to the delivery team; completed before appointment" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_capability_capacity_review ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONSIBLE_FOR ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_appointing_party .

iso:rel_920 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex B" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Informative (Annex B)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_categorization ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_classification_safety .

iso:rel_921 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex B" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Informative (Annex B)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_categorization ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_classification_security .

iso:rel_922 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex B" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Informative (Annex B)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_categorization ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_classification_environmental .

iso:rel_923 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex B" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Informative (Annex B)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_categorization ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_classification_commercial .

iso:rel_924 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex B" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Informative (Annex B)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_categorization ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_classification_operational .

iso:rel_925 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex B" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "Informative (Annex B)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_hs_categorization ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_classification_social .

iso:rel_926 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex B" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive. The codes 323 unintended collapse, 333 machinery guarding, 334 loss of control, 353 struck by machinery or part and 354 overturning plant or moving machinery are all direct consequences of EQUIPMENT OR STRUCTURAL FAILURE. Registering incidents against these codes allows the effectiveness of a predictive maintenance programme to be measured by a safety metric, not only by a downtime metric." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_failure_history ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_classification_safety .

iso:rel_927 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex B" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: the ONLY sub-value under the security group of Annex B is '41 : Connected plant and machinery'. This is where the safety axis of Part 6 touches the security axis of Part 5 directly: equipment networked in order to serve condition monitoring is classified by the SAFETY classification itself as a distinct risk group. The sensor infrastructure of a predictive maintenance system is itself a hazard to be registered, not merely a tool for reducing hazards." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_cyber_physical_system ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_classification_security .

iso:rel_928 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex B" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive. The sub-group '12 : Mechanical effect' contains 121 noise and 123 vibration - exactly the two quantities a condition monitoring system measures to detect equipment degradation. One sensor serves two purposes, and one threshold can carry two different meanings: an equipment failure threshold and an operator exposure threshold." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_condition_monitoring_system ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_classification_health .

iso:rel_929 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Annex B" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: the same class of consequence seen from two axes - term_downtime_impact (ISO 19650-3, A.4.5) measures the financial impact of asset unavailability." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_downtime_impact ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_classification_commercial .

iso:rel_93 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.3.3; Figure 7" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "information checking during information exchange between the end of one project delivery stage and the start of the next" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_exchange ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_information_verification_validation .

iso:rel_930 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "6.2: in preparing the information standard and the information production methods and procedures, the appointing party shall consider: the ability for information to be exchanged AUTOMATICALLY between geometric, construction sequenced and work planning models, spreadsheets and text documents; INTEROPERABILITY BETWEEN THE AIM AND THE PIM, and with applications which supply risk information to workers dealing with risks on site; THE POTENTIAL FOR PARTIES TO AUTOMATICALLY EXTRACT information on relevant incidents; and the need for coordination of risk information and responses." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_project_information_standard ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SPECIFIED_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_931 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The asset-side branch of the same 6.2 requirement." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_information_standard ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SPECIFIED_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_932 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.2; 5.4.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "5.4.2: the process methods and procedures to be considered are a) health and safety risk management processes and the monitoring of their effectiveness, b) collaborative sharing, review and use of health and safety information on risks and remaining levels of risk including accepted treatments and risk studies and hazard analyses, and c) responsibilities, skills and training on health and safety risk management." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_project_information_production_methods_procedures ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SPECIFIED_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_933 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.2; 5.4.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The asset-side branch of the same requirement." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_information_production_methods_procedures ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SPECIFIED_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_934 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "REUSES the Part 3 node. 6.3: the appointing party SHALL include existing health and safety information in the reference information and shared resources made available to their prospective lead appointed parties; this should include any information the appointing party already has, or can reasonably obtain, which is important to understanding the risks and risk context of the project. The NOTE gives examples: survey data, an asbestos management plan, an existing risk register, and risks adjacent to the site including vulnerable populations or hazardous access." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_reference_information_shared_resources ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_935 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.4" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "REUSES the Part 3 node (whose normative definition is at ISO 19650-2, 3.1.1.1). 6.4: in establishing acceptance criteria as part of its invitation to tender or request for service, the appointing party shall consider a) open sharing of health and safety information, b) collaborative behaviours around risk management and the sharing of risk and incident information, c) requirements for coordinating information needed from specialist sub-contractors, for example temporary works, to ensure collaboration ACROSS CONTRACTUAL BOUNDARIES, and d) evidence required to monitor and demonstrate compliance through LEADING OR LIVE INDICATORS." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_acceptance_criteria ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_936 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "6.5: as part of its delivery team mobilization, each lead appointed party SHALL identify health and safety information shortfalls and gaps that can prevent or compromise effective delivery and health and safety risk management." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_mobilization_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_information_gap .

iso:rel_937 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.1; 6.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The operational-phase branch: 6.1 requires health and safety information to be managed in accordance with ISO 19650-2 OR ISO 19650-3, so the 6.5 requirement applies to both mobilization activities." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_mobilization ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_information_gap .

iso:rel_938 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.5" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive. This is the only normative requirement in the series obliging a party to identify explicitly what it DOES NOT KNOW about risk. It corresponds directly to the missing-data problem in prediction modelling: a model trained on a dataset with systematic gaps will be confidently wrong exactly where it is most dangerous. Registering gaps as records allows a model's uncertainty to be represented as an entity in the graph." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_asset_performance_prediction ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_information_gap .

iso:rel_939 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.6; 4.5.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "6.6 and 4.5.1: as the project information model or the asset information model is created, enhanced or modified, the health and safety information SHALL be reviewed to see whether changes or additions are required across the affected parts, THEIR INTERFACES and THEIR DEPENDENCIES." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_collaborative_production_of_information_delivery ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_94 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.3.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: the risk assessment concerns delivery of asset or project information, which is planned through information delivery plans; clause 6.3.1 says a documented information-delivery risk assessment should be included in the overall asset or project risk assessment, but does not state this exact edge" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_delivery_plan ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_information_delivery_risk_assessment .

iso:rel_940 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.1; 6.6" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "The operational-phase branch of the same 6.6 requirement." ;
    rdf:object iso:activity_production_of_information ;
    rdf:predicate iso:APPLIES_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_941 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.1; 6.6; Introduction" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    rdf:object iso:term_pim ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_942 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "5.2; 6.6; Introduction" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK. Introduction: during handover and close out of the project, the health and safety information is used to ensure that the PIM is used to UPDATE THE AIM, and is handed over to those who will be responsible for managing and assessing health and safety risks during the operational phase. 5.2 b) reinforces this: the AIR shall ensure that information generated in a delivery or in-use phase is available during subsequent phases." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_aim ;
    rdf:predicate iso:PART_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_health_safety_information .

iso:rel_943 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "6.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "PdM HOOK: interpretive. 6.2 requires consideration of 'the potential for parties to AUTOMATICALLY EXTRACT information on relevant incidents'. Automatic extraction of incident data for analysis is precisely the information synthesis step of ISO 19650-5, B.4.2 d) - and therefore attracts the same information security policies, including the change-control requirement on synthesis technology at B.4.1 f)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_lifecycle_synthesis ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_incident .

iso:rel_944 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.4; Table 3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: an incident at the Operation stage typically leads to corrective maintenance work - trigger_maintenance_work of ISO 19650-3, A.3 is defined as 'maintenance work on an asset, whether planned or REACTIVE'." ;
    rdf:object iso:trigger_maintenance_work ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESULTS_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_incident .

iso:rel_945 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.4; Table 3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: an incident with a Very high consequence per Table C.3 corresponds to trigger_emergency_response of ISO 19650-3, A.3 and to the 'very urgent' priority level of Table C.3." ;
    rdf:object iso:trigger_emergency_response ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESULTS_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_incident .

iso:rel_946 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.3; Table 2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: the Review date field of Table 2 (the date a review is due or has been carried out) creates a time-based risk review schedule, corresponding to trigger_asset_inspection of ISO 19650-3, A.3 and to term_maintenance_inspection_schedule of A.4.1." ;
    rdf:object iso:trigger_asset_inspection ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESULTS_IN ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_risk .

iso:rel_947 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.5.1; 6.6" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: the requirement to review the health and safety information EVERY TIME a model is created, enhanced or modified (4.5.1, 6.6) is a mechanism for keeping model content aligned with reality - corresponding to term_aim_asset_alignment of ISO 19650-3, 5.1.12 Note 2 (the interval between changes occurring to the asset and those changes being reflected in the AIM)." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_aim_asset_alignment ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUPPORTS ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_hs_information_sharing .

iso:rel_948 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.3.2; Table 1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: the Associated activity field of Table 1 takes as its value an 'asset life cycle stage or work package'; term_information_delivery_milestone (ISO 19650-2, 3.1.3.2) is the scheduled event tied to those stages, allowing a risk record to be anchored to the project's information delivery schedule." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information_delivery_milestone ;
    rdf:predicate iso:LINKED_TO ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_context_sub_schema .

iso:rel_949 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "Introduction; 5.2" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "INTERPRETIVE: ISO 19650-1, 7.2 states that asset information management should be involved in ALL stages of project delivery, because handover information must include what is required for operation and maintenance; the Part 6 Introduction states that health and safety information is handed over to those who will be responsible for managing and assessing health and safety risks during the operational phase. Both sentences describe the same function." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_health_safety_information ;
    rdf:predicate iso:RESPONSIBLE_FOR ;
    rdf:subject iso:function_asset_information_management .

iso:rel_95 a rdf:Statement ;
    iso:provenanceClause "3.2.9" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-1" ;
    iso:relationshipNote "3.2.9 defines project information as 'information (3.3.1) produced for, or utilized in, a particular project'." ;
    rdf:object iso:term_information ;
    rdf:predicate iso:SUBTYPE_OF ;
    rdf:subject iso:term_project_information .

iso:rel_950 a rdf:Statement ;
