    iso:definition "policies and processes relating to personnel security which should consider including: identification of high-risk functions within the organization(s) and any organizations employed as part of an appointment or providing services; security screening and vetting requirements for any individual(s) in contact with sensitive assets, including information, both in general and specific roles; security competence requirements of individuals in specific roles; induction of all new personnel and organizations providing services so that they are appropriately briefed on their responsibilities and the required security-minded culture, including general security awareness training provided and recorded as part of a project or ongoing operations alongside health and safety, project or site familiarization and other similar training, and the mandatory topics and required learning outcomes of those sessions; general security awareness and training requirements including refresher training; role-based security training requirements; ongoing security training and awareness requirements; access and permission requirements to information and information models; and demobilization of organization(s) and personnel" ;
    iso:nodeId "term_personnel_security_control" ;
    iso:part "ISO 19650-5" ;
    iso:pdmRelevance "medium" ;
    iso:provenanceClause "B.1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-5" ;
    iso:sourceType "informative_annex" .

