    iso:definition "potential for the aggregation of information to lead to the identification of individuals or groups of individuals, to reveal sensitive information about initiatives, projects, assets, products, services, individuals or communities, or to reveal information about the configuration of assets, products, components and/or software in a system; arises from aggregation by accumulation, where the volume of information stored together increases the level of impact that would occur if the information was compromised; from aggregation by association, where the association of different types of information, which in themselves have little or no impact when compromised, have a higher level of impact when associated together; or from a combination of accumulation and association" ;
    iso:nodeId "term_information_aggregation_risk" ;
    iso:part "ISO 19650-5" ;
    iso:pdmRelevance "high" ;
    iso:provenanceClause "A.1 g); A.1 NOTE 5; 7.2.3 b); C.3" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-5" ;
    iso:sourceType "mixed_normative_informative" .

