    iso:definition "common method for structuring health and safety information, adopted by the appointing party to support the risk management cycle including identification, sharing, use and generalization of information and supporting evidence relating to a) health and safety risk management, b) hazard and incident management, and c) optionally, the recording of previous and existing states of the health and safety information which can affect works on the current project or asset; health and safety context, risks, incidents and treatments shall be described using the sub-schemas of 4.3.2 to 4.3.5 or as identified in the project/asset information standard" ;
    iso:nodeId "term_hs_schema" ;
    iso:part "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:pdmRelevance "high" ;
    iso:provenanceClause "4.2.1; 4.3.1; Figure 1" ;
    iso:provenanceStandard "ISO 19650-6" ;
    iso:sourceType "body_clause" .

